WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.170
Shifts brings two kinds of scheduling into one place.

00:00:03.589 --> 00:00:06.619
Recurring Group Shifts organizes people and required

00:00:06.650 --> 00:00:08.529
roles across dated shift days.

00:00:08.949 --> 00:00:12.880
Add Static Shift creates a separate fixed window for resources.

00:00:13.340 --> 00:00:15.920
Start by identifying the work you need to coordinate.

00:00:16.340 --> 00:00:20.319
In our fictional Chicago Fire department, we will create an assigned personnel

00:00:20.319 --> 00:00:22.940
schedule, then a separate signup schedule.

00:00:23.420 --> 00:00:28.530
Your Shifts, On Duty Now, Approvals and Shift Staffing are separate views.

00:00:28.950 --> 00:00:32.509
A scheduled roster gives you recorded coverage; check current

00:00:32.509 --> 00:00:34.430
operational information separately.

00:00:34.610 --> 00:00:37.000
Choose Add Recurring Group Shift to

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:43.259
open New Shift. Enter a distinctive practice name and the short code T R N twenty-eight A.

00:00:43.709 --> 00:00:46.900
Assignment Type is Assigned, so the administrator chooses

00:00:46.900 --> 00:00:48.299
the people for this schedule.

00:00:48.730 --> 00:00:52.060
Use a light background color because the calendar text is black.

00:00:52.469 --> 00:00:55.769
The supervisor approval checkbox is clear in this example.

00:00:56.139 --> 00:01:00.900
That control governs signups and trades; it is not the list of assigned personnel.

00:01:01.320 --> 00:01:04.769
Review these choices before using Next to open Schedule.

00:01:04.960 --> 00:01:08.450
Schedule gives you a multi-month date picker and separate Start

00:01:08.450 --> 00:01:10.039
Time and End Time fields.

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:13.859
Our example selects November fourth, twenty twenty-six, from

00:01:13.859 --> 00:01:15.449
nine to eleven in the morning.

00:01:15.920 --> 00:01:19.380
Check both displayed times after leaving the fields and confirm

00:01:19.380 --> 00:01:20.990
the intended date is highlighted.

00:01:21.419 --> 00:01:24.779
This is a manually selected schedule, even though it appears

00:01:24.779 --> 00:01:26.289
under Recurring Group Shifts.

00:01:26.599 --> 00:01:29.830
The wizard shown here does not offer a rotation preset.

00:01:30.289 --> 00:01:33.849
Once the date and times are correct, continue to the Slots stage.

00:01:34.029 --> 00:01:37.210
In Slots, Add Group to Shift adds a group row.

00:01:37.630 --> 00:01:39.750
Firehouse fifty-one is selected here.

00:01:40.219 --> 00:01:43.909
Add Role to Group creates a required-role row for that group.

00:01:44.399 --> 00:01:47.250
Choose Officer and leave Roles Count at one.

00:01:47.689 --> 00:01:50.239
These values define what coverage the schedule should

00:01:50.239 --> 00:01:51.780
compare against its roster.

00:01:52.190 --> 00:01:54.840
Adding a role minimum does not assign a person.

00:01:55.290 --> 00:01:59.559
Review the group, role and count together, then continue to Personnel.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:03.030
Use the department’s published role conventions when configuring

00:02:03.030 --> 00:02:04.700
your own coverage requirements.

00:02:04.800 --> 00:02:08.999
Personnel separates Non-Group Personnel from the individual group pickers.

00:02:09.560 --> 00:02:12.959
Non-group entries are described as floaters or standbys.

00:02:13.510 --> 00:02:16.909
In the Firehouse fifty-one picker, choose Matthew Casey.

00:02:17.329 --> 00:02:19.529
His selected name is visible as a chip.

00:02:20.010 --> 00:02:23.109
Leave the other group pickers empty for this small exercise.

00:02:23.609 --> 00:02:27.209
The text explains that assigned people fill role slots according

00:02:27.209 --> 00:02:28.550
to their group and roles.

00:02:29.050 --> 00:02:33.000
Verify the selected member under the intended group; selecting a name

00:02:33.050 --> 00:02:34.820
elsewhere is a different assignment.

00:02:35.289 --> 00:02:37.450
Use Next when that review is complete.

00:02:37.679 --> 00:02:40.939
The Finish stage contains an instruction and a separate Finish

00:02:40.939 --> 00:02:42.420
control at the lower right.

00:02:42.779 --> 00:02:44.869
That lower control creates the schedule.

00:02:45.290 --> 00:02:47.000
Submit once and read the

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:48.969
returned row in Recurring Group Shifts.

00:02:49.370 --> 00:02:53.659
Our new row says Assigned and Manual, with one group and one person.

00:02:54.089 --> 00:02:58.890
It offers View Calendar, Edit Details, Edit Calendar and Edit Groups.

00:02:59.190 --> 00:03:02.210
Those actions inspect different parts of the saved schedule.

00:03:02.620 --> 00:03:06.669
Confirm the new row before opening an editor or assuming that a prepared

00:03:06.669 --> 00:03:08.300
wizard has already been stored.

00:03:08.550 --> 00:03:10.000
Reopen Edit Details

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:13.179
to check the stored name, code, light blue color

00:03:13.249 --> 00:03:15.010
and nine-to-eleven time window.

00:03:15.409 --> 00:03:18.179
Casey remains selected under Firehouse fifty-one.

00:03:18.820 --> 00:03:21.830
In the shared calendar, open the November fourth entry.

00:03:22.219 --> 00:03:25.529
Its day detail is Upcoming and shows the same times.

00:03:25.939 --> 00:03:29.910
The Officer row says Required one and Needed zero; the

00:03:29.910 --> 00:03:32.189
roster lists Casey as Assigned.

00:03:32.689 --> 00:03:36.389
Fully staffed means this configured one-role requirement is filled.

00:03:36.750 --> 00:03:39.900
It does not establish arrival, qualifications or

00:03:39.900 --> 00:03:41.299
an apparatus crew assignment.

00:03:41.770 --> 00:03:44.200
Read the actual role counts behind the summary.

00:03:44.399 --> 00:03:49.410
For a signup schedule, create a separate practice entry with code T R N

00:03:49.519 --> 00:03:52.549
twenty-eight S and Assignment Type Signup.

00:03:53.240 --> 00:03:56.330
Check Signups and trades need supervisor approval.

00:03:56.729 --> 00:04:00.680
The help says that a signup or trade does not put anyone on duty until

00:04:00.680 --> 00:04:02.410
a group supervisor approves it.

00:04:02.850 --> 00:04:07.000
Select November fifth and sixth, using the same morning time window

00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:09.609
and one required Officer for Firehouse fifty-one.

00:04:10.160 --> 00:04:12.139
Leave every Personnel picker empty.

00:04:12.500 --> 00:04:14.820
Members can request their own dates separately.

00:04:15.279 --> 00:04:18.159
Review Finish and submit this new schedule once.

00:04:18.379 --> 00:04:21.260
The saved row now carries Approval required.

00:04:21.679 --> 00:04:26.000
Reopen its details and calendar to verify the setting, times and two

00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:27.009
selected dates.

00:04:27.490 --> 00:04:29.000
On November fifth, the

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:31.139
day detail is Signup and Upcoming.

00:04:31.469 --> 00:04:34.979
It shows Open slots one, an Officer requirement of one,

00:04:35.299 --> 00:04:37.299
and Nobody is on this day yet.

00:04:37.660 --> 00:04:41.219
Your Status says that the current user is not on this day, and a

00:04:41.219 --> 00:04:42.979
group signup button is available.

00:04:43.340 --> 00:04:47.410
An empty roster remains unfilled even though the schedule has been created.

00:04:47.779 --> 00:04:51.739
A member request and its supervisor review are separate operations.

00:04:51.949 --> 00:04:56.550
Department Shift Settings has a separate Allow Signups For Multiple Groups option.

00:04:57.030 --> 00:04:59.349
It is off here and remains unchanged.

00:04:59.769 --> 00:05:03.810
The help asks you to review overlaps and local coverage rules separately.

00:05:04.260 --> 00:05:06.909
This department policy is different from the approval

00:05:06.909 --> 00:05:08.920
checkbox on an individual shift.

00:05:09.450 --> 00:05:11.000
Open Approvals to review

00:05:11.000 --> 00:05:13.760
waiting signups and trades in groups you supervise.

00:05:14.170 --> 00:05:16.149
Both queues are empty in this example.

00:05:16.600 --> 00:05:19.950
The page states that a pending request does not put anyone

00:05:19.950 --> 00:05:21.790
on duty until it is approved.

00:05:22.190 --> 00:05:24.859
An empty queue is not a completed approval.

00:05:25.040 --> 00:05:28.089
On Duty Now shows a timestamp and the currently active

00:05:28.089 --> 00:05:29.869
shift, grouped by assignment.

00:05:30.300 --> 00:05:34.790
Here the existing A Shift is active, with its recorded members and roles.

00:05:35.210 --> 00:05:37.689
Our new November dates are future schedules.

00:05:38.050 --> 00:05:41.960
Keep those two questions separate: who is scheduled on a selected day,

00:05:42.220 --> 00:05:44.009
and which schedule is active now.

00:05:44.439 --> 00:05:48.320
The page says it refreshes every minute and also offers Refresh.

00:05:48.720 --> 00:05:53.009
These are recorded roster views; use the appropriate operational workflow

00:05:53.009 --> 00:05:56.800
to verify current availability and other information your team needs.

00:05:56.880 --> 00:06:00.560
Chicago Fire can use this pattern to coordinate station coverage.

00:06:00.979 --> 00:06:04.539
Community care and mental health teams can schedule operational team

00:06:04.539 --> 00:06:06.419
coverage without patient detail.

00:06:06.770 --> 00:06:11.109
Search and rescue can organize standby roles; security teams can coordinate

00:06:11.109 --> 00:06:16.029
site coverage; wildland crews can plan relief rosters; and industrial response

00:06:16.029 --> 00:06:17.750
teams can schedule drill support.

00:06:18.230 --> 00:06:22.019
In every setting, choose the right assignment type, state the group

00:06:22.050 --> 00:06:26.199
and role requirements clearly, and verify the saved dated roster.

00:06:26.630 --> 00:06:30.389
Handle member requests, approvals, attendance and trades through

00:06:30.389 --> 00:06:31.999
their own reviewed steps.

